E('By contrast, **Fig. 3a** shows no strain recovery of the LLM-alloy during this test, indicating that it deforms plastically with no pseudo-elasticity regardless of heat-treating condition. We conclude that the microstructure of the LLM-alloy is very stable and that stress-induced phase transformation is not one of its active deformation mechanisms.',
  'By contrast, **Fig. 3a** shows no strain recovery of the LLM-alloy during this test. The test is reported for one condition of the LLM-alloy, 1200 °C for 1 minute — the same anneal as the benchmark panel — and what it establishes is confined to that state, the γ-majority γ + α duplex quantified in Sec. 3.3: no stress-induced martensite stable enough to survive unloading was present to revert on heating. The unloading evidence is broader, since in each of the eight conditions of **Fig. 2** the unloading segment returns no strain beyond the elastic σ/E. Within the conditions reported here, then, the LLM-alloy deforms plastically with no resolvable pseudo-elastic contribution, shows no shape-memory recovery in the one state given the heating test, and stress-induced phase transformation is not among its active deformation mechanisms as processed here.')
